From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Sun, 28 Jun 2026 19:05:10 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 04737/11362] [outer-loop] In-context verified-pattern lever:
 POWERED NULL on behavior patterns (n=19 LOO, M=5)

Operator 2026-06-28: "ignoring the obfuscated source code, we do have offlinesolves
we have RE'd that can be broken down and analyzed." Isolated the RE'd SEMANTIC solve
knowledge (registry win_condition/action_model/gotchas + solve trajectories + dead_ends),
source EXCLUDED, and ran the cheapest-decisive LOO proposal-shift A/B properly powered.

RESULT: in-context exemplars do NOT reliably shift the small LLM's proposed opening
toward a held-out game's banked winner. leading delta +0.042 CI95 [-0.095,+0.211]
(spans 0); degeneracy-robust LCS delta -0.076 CI95 [-0.208,+0.026] (spans 0, leans
negative); exemplars_help=False. Apparent gains concentrate on all-click [6,6,6,6]
winners (coincidental click-nudging), offset by hurts elsewhere -- not transferable.
Matches WALL_IS_HIDDEN_STATE + arc_solve_learning.py:114. Source-code half independently
obfuscation-blocked (13/25 source patterns semantically empty). Supersedes the earlier
n=8/M=3 AMBIGUOUS read; both halves of the 2026-06-28 lever now closed.

- harness: added LCS (degeneracy-robust) co-primary metric, M-sample denoising,
  per-game checkpoint/resume (survives the ~5min kill window), powered-null verdict,
  honest aggregation_from_upstream_artifacts substrate (cites 19 live-LLM checkpoints).
- adversarial_verify clean (0 flags); adversarial sub-agent review APPROVE; 7 unit tests pass.
- ledger updated (arc-agi3-levers-tried-x-verdict-2026-06-25.md): behavior half = powered null.

